<item>
            <title>[BOOKKEEPER-899] Bookie should return to read-write mode once the disk usage drops before the threshold</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/BOOKKEEPER-899</link>
                <project id="12311293" key="BOOKKEEPER">Bookkeeper</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Once a bookie goes above the diskUsageThreshold and becomes readOnly, it will never go back to readWrite even if the disk usage drops significantly.&lt;br/&gt;
When the LedgerDirsMonitor gets a NoWritableLedgerDirException, it will put the bookie in read only mode, but will also stop monitoring and never goes back to read-write mode when the disk usage drops below threshold.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Solution:&lt;br/&gt;
The LedgerDirsMonitor thread should not break out of the while loop when it gets NoWritableLedgerDirException, and should continue monitoring the directories.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
